From: iOSPlus10 kernel agent (power)
Subject: [PATCH] negroni cpuidle: OSI cluster states, RPMh sleep/wake sets, sleep stats (0383)

Findings: every logged boot ran negronicpuidle=0 (WFI only). Under Gunyah a vCPU in WFI stays "active"
for the PSCI aggregation (quic/gunyah-hypervisor psci_osi_handle_idle_yield), so no core, cluster or
APSS power-down ever happened and the APSS RSC never sent a sleep set: CX and XO cannot drop.

- negronicpuidle=3: SET_SUSPEND_MODE(OSI) at start (Linux psci_set_osi_mode; Gunyah gives the HLOS
  FEATURES(CPU_SUSPEND) = 3); the last core passes the cluster param when the earliest deadline of all
  cores fits the cluster residency (Linux genpd + cpuidle-psci-domain). DENIED -> 4 idles core-only.
  If the switch fails, level 3 = level 2 (PC, each core asks, Gunyah aggregates).
- llcc-off (cluster-e3) only with negronicpuidle_llcc=1 (default 0); l3-off with level >= 2.
- Before any cluster param: negroni_rpmh_sleep_ready() (RPMh DRV idle, sets current; Linux
  rpmh_rsc_pd_cb at the cluster PRE_OFF).
- bsd/dev/negroni_rpmh.c: read-only dump of the 8 DRV2 TCS at first use; a cache of every ACTIVE vote;
  negronirpmh_sleep (default 0 = never written): 1 = Linux rules (sleep != wake only: BCM keepalive
  -> 0), 2 = + ARC level 0 / BCM 0 in sleep. SLEEP TCS 3-4, WAKE TCS 5-6 (live.dts qcom,tcs-config),
  rewritten in thread context after each changed vote, WAKE first.
- Read-only stats every 60 s (negronicpuidle_stats, default 7 at level >= 1; at level 0 only when
  given): AOP rpmh-sleep-stats (aosd/cxsd/ddr count + time), DDR LPM counts, CPUSS C4/D4 counters.

