+++ b/osfmk/arm64/negroni_cpuidle.c
@@ -42,6 +42,27 @@
  * shorter than the residency -> the next 8 idles of that core are WFI.
  * Log: "NEGRONI CPUIDLE: ..." at start, then every 60 s one line per core and state:
  * "NEGRONI CPUIDLE: cpuN state S param 0x... entered N times: ...".
+ *
+ * Patch 0383 (cluster states as Linux, RPMh sleep sets, sleep statistics):
+ * - Gunyah (the hypervisor) implements PSCI for the HLOS VM (quic/gunyah-hypervisor hyp/vm/psci_osi): FEATURES
+ *   (CPU_SUSPEND) = 3 for the HLOS (OSI + extended StateID), the VM starts in PC mode, a vCPU in WFI stays "active"
+ *   for the aggregation, so the physical core only clock-gates (psci_osi_handle_idle_yield: no suspend while an
+ *   affine vCPU is active). Only CPU_SUSPEND lets Gunyah power the core, the cluster (L3) or the APSS down.
+ * - negronicpuidle=3: OS-initiated mode, as Linux cpuidle-psci-domain (psci_pd_init_topology -> psci_set_osi_mode):
+ *   SET_SUSPEND_MODE(OSI) at start (Gunyah allows it while every other vCPU is active = here, before ci_ready), then
+ *   the last core (every other core inside CPU_SUSPEND) passes the cluster param when the earliest deadline of all
+ *   cores is at least the cluster residency away (the genpd governor's next wakeup); the others pass the core param.
+ *   Gunyah answers DENIED when its view differs (osi_mode_suspend_state_validation_at_level): counted, then 4 idles
+ *   core-only. If SET_SUSPEND_MODE fails, level 3 works as level 2 (PC).
+ * - Before any cluster param: negroni_rpmh_sleep_ready() (bsd/dev/negroni_rpmh.c) must say the RPMh DRV is idle and
+ *   its SLEEP/WAKE sets are current (Linux rpmh_rsc_pd_cb at the cluster PRE_OFF); else the core param.
